      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "No, there is no safe \"middle ground\" because iron toxicity is a straight line to organ failure, not a gradual improvement.\nTaking even 200mg when prescribed less is still a dangerous overdose that can cause severe nausea, vomiting, and permanent liver damage.\nYour son's exhaustion is a sign he needs the exact prescribed dose, not a risky guess, and pushing it higher will only make the situation worse.\nPlease stop trying to self-adjust the dosage and call his doctor immediately to discuss a faster follow-up or alternative treatment plan.",
